I ask the shopkeeper for a shirt bigger than this.
The shopkeeper nods.
He looks on the shelf.
He gives me another shirt of the same color.
"Madam, look at this size," he says.
"This is bigger than that shirt."
I take the shirt and say thank you.
There is a big mirror near the wall of the shop.
I go near the mirror.
This time I do not want to make any mistake.
I want to try on the new shirt.
There is no changing room in the shop.
So I put the new shirt on right over my t-shirt.
I look at myself in the mirror.
I move my shoulders to check.
Now this is looking absolutely fine.
This new shirt is much better than the small one.
